Replacing and Merging Objects with Drag-and-Drop
While creating your simulation model , you can replace or merge objects with drag-and-drop.
You can:
• Replace an instance with a class
Hold down Alt while dragging the class object on the instance and dropping it there. This way you
can, for example, replace a Station with an AssemblyStation. Plant Simulation preserves all connected
Connectors, but deletes all MUs on the object.
Note
Plant Simulation also lets you copy the attribute values of the previous instance into the new
instance. When you select to not do this, the new instance is in the same state as an instance you
inserted from the Class Library, i.e., all built-in attributes are inherited and all user-defined attributes
and sensors, which you defined in the previous instance, will be discarded.
Note
When replacing an instance of an object with the class of another object, Plant Simulation retains the
existing name. This prevents you from having to change the existing name in a control or a table, for
example.
• Merge classes
Hold Alt and the left mouse button down. Then drag the replacing object in the Class Library over the
class to be replaced, and drop it there.
Compare Merge Classes, Example
Compare Exchange Classes, Example
