Add Basic Objects to the Class Library or Remove Them from It
You can add the built-in objects, which are part of your program package, to the Class Library and to the
Toolbox in the dialog Manage Class Library.
Proceed as follows:
• Select the objects, which you need for creating the current and future simulation models.
Clear the check box for the objects, which you do not need.
• Click Apply to add the selected objects to the Class Library and to the Toolbox or to remove them from
it.
• If you want Plant Simulation to always show this dialog, when you open a new model, select the check
box Always Show This Dialog When You Open a New Model. Then you can configure each simulation
Add Basic Objects to the Class Library or Remove Them from It
